The linker error `undefined reference to __device_dts_ord_32` indicates that a device node defined in the devicetree is not being claimed by any driver, thus its corresponding device object (and its linker-generated symbol `__device_dts_ord_XX`) is not created.

In `tests/drivers/fuel_gauge/bq40z50/boards/native_sim.overlay`, the `bq40z50` node is defined as a child of `&i2c0` but lacks a `compatible` property:

```overlay
&i2c0 {
	bq40z50: bq40z50@16 {
		reg = <0x16>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
```

The test `tests/drivers/fuel_gauge/bq40z50/src/test_bq40z50.c` uses `DEVICE_DT_GET_ANY(ti_bq40z50)`, which expects a device with `compatible = "ti,bq40z50"`. The `rpi_pico.overlay` for the same test correctly specifies this compatible string.

By adding `compatible = "ti,bq40z50"` to the `bq40z50` node in `native_sim.overlay`, the `ti,bq40z50` driver will claim this device node, leading to the creation of the necessary device object and its linker symbol, thus resolving the `undefined reference` error.

